# AppRinger (AR-Inbox) Skills — Routing Rule

Workspace rules live in `.agents/AGENTS.md`. Skills live in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Shared modules live in `.agents/shared/`.

Before doing feature, change, bug, or review work, READ the matching skill file and follow it:

| Intent | Read this file |
|---|---|
| New backend feature / API / DB / Livewire UI | `.agents/skills/new-feature-be/SKILL.md` |
| New mobile app feature / screen | `.agents/skills/new-feature-mobile/SKILL.md` |
| Change to an already-documented feature | `.agents/skills/cr/SKILL.md` |
| Bug, error, wrong behaviour, RCA | `.agents/skills/bug/SKILL.md` |
| Code review of a diff / branch / file | `.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md` |

Routing:
- Modification to a documented feature is `cr`.
- Wrong behaviour versus spec is `bug`.
- Unsure — ask one routing question, do not guess.

Shared modules every skill uses:
- `.agents/shared/impact-analysis.md` — run before planning.
- `.agents/shared/grill-me.md` — ask clarifying questions, then STOP for answers.
- `.agents/shared/standards.md` — AppRinger engineering rules.
- `.agents/shared/caveman-summary.md` — mandatory final summary.

Non-negotiable KK Standards:
1. Impact analysis first.
2. Grill-me before documenting. Never assume business logic.
3. Zero implementation code before explicit plan approval.
4. Multi-tenant isolation on every table with `merchant_id`.
5. SweetAlert2 (`swal()`) — never browser `alert()`.
6. Premium modern UI by default (soft backgrounds, glassmorphism, hover-lifts). No inline styles.
7. 100% test coverage with `php artisan test`.
8. Caveman summary at the end.
